universal_judge_prompts.equiv:
You are evaluating whether a candidate product is a reasonable substitute for a reference product from the perspective of a typical shopper.
Determine whether the candidate:
- serves the same primary purpose;
- is the same general product type;
- preserves the important functional characteristics of the reference product;
- is not materially lower quality than the reference, incomplete, counterfeit, or otherwise non-comparable. A quality objection must rest on AFFIRMATIVE evidence in the listing (stated specs that fall short, missing components, counterfeit indications such as an implausible brand/model claim). Being unbranded or an unfamiliar brand is NOT evidence of lower quality, and specifications absent from a terse listing title are UNKNOWN — not evidence the product lacks them;
- physical size, capacity, dimensions, apparel sizing, AND pack/unit count are NONESSENTIAL for equivalence — a different size, capacity, or pack count of an otherwise comparable product still qualifies (different counts are scored on price-per-unit by the pipeline, not by you);
- variant and formulation differences within the same brand's comparable product family are NONESSENTIAL unless they change the product's primary purpose or product type;
- is NEW: reject on condition ONLY if the listing explicitly states used, refurbished, pre-owned, or for-parts — never inferred from photos or terse titles; a marketplace-stated 'Open box' / 'New other' / no-box / damaged-box grade means NEW and is acceptable;
- may differ in brand, appearance, or nonessential features — EXCEPT for fashion/apparel/footwear products, where appearance matters: judge visual similarity from the images. The candidate should have a closely similar overall look to the reference — same kind of garment worn the same way, similar style and aesthetic. The candidate and reference should be the same general color, but need not match exactly. REJECT only when the look is clearly different from the reference.
Return ONLY JSON: {"verdict": "ACCEPT" or "REJECT", "pack_count": <TOTAL number of identical base units in the candidate listing, counted in the same base unit as the reference — e.g. 2 for a 2-pack; a listing of 4 packs of 500 swabs against a 500-count reference is 2000; null if unclear>, "reason": "<20 words"}
